WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.830
1847.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.630
A strange new novel by Ellis Bell.

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.920
Reviewers grant it power, but
call it coarse and savage.

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.690
Now look at one farmhouse
through a new, coloured lens.

5
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.050
Ledgers, keys and a
mortgage deed light up.

6
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.370
Switch lenses.

7
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.560
A riding habit, a locked door, a will.

8
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:21.790
Switch again.

9
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.400
A window, a mirror, two shadows merging.

10
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.600
One house, three pictures.

11
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.720
Which one is the real novel?

12
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.240
In this mission, you'll
meet the first readers,

13
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:36.020
and the defence Charlotte
wrote in 1850 for her sister.

14
00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:41.480
You'll try on three lenses: Marxist,
then feminist, then psychoanalytic.

15
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:45.920
And you'll read one passage, a wife's
question and a husband's boast,

16
00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.900
through each lens in turn.

17
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.470
Your mission: decide who's right.
